// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO14 tagged "led_low" - confirmed onboard programmable
// indicator LED, active-low. M5Stack Unit CamS3 product page PinMap
// (docs.m5stack.com/en/unit/Unit-CamS3) lists "Programmable LED" on G14.
// Polarity (active-low/inverted) corroborated by two independent
// third-party sources using the same GPIO14 LED circuit: M5Stack's own
// ESPHome/Home Assistant integration for the sibling Unit CamS3-5MP
// (docs.m5stack.com/en/homeassistant/camera/unit_cams3_5mp) configures
// GPIO14 as a switch with "inverted: true", and the Tasmota community
// template (templates.blakadder.com/m5stack_unitcams3.html) maps GPIO14
// to "Led_i" (Tasmota's inverted-LED component). No physical button was
// found in any consulted source, so nothing was tagged as a button - see
// boardsDetails/esp32/esp32s3/m5stack_unit_cams3/notes.txt. This is a
// full copy of variants/esp32/esp32s3/board.json (chip-level default)
// with only GPIO14's capabilities modified; no per-board pin-exclusion
// audit was performed in this pass.
